# Goal
# Straight-line Cartesian move along the tool's OWN +Z axis (the gripper's approach
# direction), holding the current orientation. Relative rather than absolute so the
# caller cannot specify a path that leaves the approach axis: the same action serves
# the pre-grasp approach (positive) and the retreat (negative).
float64 distance     # meters, signed: + moves the fingertips forward, - backs them off
float32 speed        # m/s translation ceiling; 0.0 uses the controller's default
---
# Result
bool success
---
# Feedback
float64 distance_to_go
